## Flags for the release VM (`mix release` renders this file; see
## https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html).

## No scheduler busy-waiting. A container under a CPU quota pays for the spin
## as throttled time, and the edge's work arrives in bursts anyway.
+sbwt none
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none

## The distribution listener binds loopback only (epmd is pinned to loopback by
## ERL_EPMD_ADDRESS in env.sh.eex): `bin/ankusa remote` and `rpc` work from
## inside the container, nothing outside it can connect.
-kernel inet_dist_use_interface {127,0,0,1}

## Shell history for `remote` sessions, kept under $HOME (the data volume).
-kernel shell_history enabled
